cpuz_arm64.exe
    CPU-Z for Windows ARM64, (c) CPUID, https://www.cpuid.com/. It is
    redistributed unmodified in this project's GitHub releases, and fetched at
    release time from https://download.cpuid.com/cpu-z/arm64/, purely so that
    `cpuz-bench --official` can score aarch64 builds with CPUID's own benchmark
    kernel instead of our LLVM build of the same algorithm. It is not part of
    this project's source and carries no license from us; all rights remain
    with CPUID. Remove it if CPUID objects.
    The `q-cpuz-benchmark` wrapper in the author's dotfiles downloads it into
    the local cache for the same purpose; nothing is executed beyond the
    benchmark kernel.

    If the file is absent, `cpuz-bench` falls back to its own engine and says
    so. To skip fetching it entirely, pass --no-official or set
    CPUZ_NO_OFFICIAL=1.

The 17.01 / 19.01 benchmark algorithms reimplemented in src/ were recovered by
disassembling CPUID's binaries for interoperability. Addresses, constant pools
and instruction shapes quoted in the docs and source comments are facts about
those binaries, included so the reimplementation can be checked against them.
